<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32381" root="غمد" body-key="g">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَكِىٌّ غَامِدٌ</span></b> , a phrase like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِيشَةٌ رَاضِيَةٌ</span>, [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَامِدٌ</span>
meaning <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَغْمُودٌ</span>,] (tropical:)  <i>Wells having their water
covered by earth,</i> or <i>dust; contr. of</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَكِىٌّ مُبْدٍ</span>.
(A.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَامِدَةٌ</span> (tropical:)  A well (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِئْرٌ</span>) <i>filled up,</i> or
<i>choked up, with earth,</i> or <i>dust.</i> (K, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَامِدَةٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَامِدٌ</span> (assumed tropical:)  A ship (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَفِينَةٌ</span>) <i>filled,</i> or
<i>laden;</i> (K, TA;) as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">آمِدَةٌ</span> (TA) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">آمِدٌ</span>.
(K, TA.)

